# Legacy project migration (7 October 2026)

- Resolve the existing project identity through `Client.mjs global-index` and its context. Retain its V2 source IDs, canonical cloud folder, dependencies, cover and feedback. An old catalogue entry is not an excuse to create a second identity. (7 October 2026)
- Read the actual legacy plan. Map each source to a stable source ID, namespace, absolute localPath and relative include selection. `files` in a shared folder becomes `include`, never the whole folder. Preserve `keep: true`. `target` is historical cloud layout, not a new source identity. (7 October 2026)
- Register the definition through the existing bridge `start` action with `id`, `project` and the existing sources. The service merges supplied source IDs and prepares canonical Memory. Never drop unrelated existing sources; resolve paths outside allowed roots explicitly instead of expanding access to a parent directory. (7 October 2026)
- Bind the real host session through BeginConversation; a session already bound to another project is not reassigned. `start` for another project can omit sessionId. Obtain the workshop from the returned setup before generating files. (7 October 2026)
- Run `Client.mjs inventory <id>`, then `Client.mjs archive <id>`; a returned jobId proves queueing only. Inspect job.state, project error and each selected file’s backup record. Archive retries pending index publication through the existing engine; there is no public reindex action. (7 October 2026)
- `Client.mjs status <id>` replaces the old status command. `Client.mjs unload-plan <id>` and `unload <id>` apply to a managed LOAD workspace. Do not substitute the legacy `free` command or purge production sources. (7 October 2026)
- An archive proof identifies the selected file, current SHA256, byte length and immutable cloud version. A LOAD or recovery proof independently compares restored bytes. File names or N/N manifest counts alone do not prove recoverability. (7 October 2026)
- Old `zr-assets-cartel.py` and its recipe stay in the historical archive. Their presentation schema is not the V2 project schema; retain useful measured presentation metadata without writing it into the live mapping. (7 October 2026)

## Verified bridge payload and per-file evidence (7 October 2026)

- Exact command from the repository: `node scripts/Assets/Client.mjs start <existing-id> '{"id":"<existing-id>","project":{"id":"<existing-id>","name":"<existing-name>","sources":[{"id":"<source-id>","namespace":"tmp","localPath":"<absolute-registered-root>","include":["first.txt","second.txt"],"keep":true}]}}'`. Replace the example with the real complete project definition and scoped paths; the outer id is required because start reads payload.id, not the target’s projectId. (7 October 2026)
- Client status and inventory print aggregate sync and jobs, not all files. Read `~/Library/Application Support/ZenRayAssets/Project-<id>.json`: `inventory.localFiles` gives sourceId and relativePath, `backups[<source-id>:<relative-path>]` gives the archived SHA256, size, cloud path and version. Compare to the CURRENT local bytes; a previous successful archive may already be stale. The authenticated bridge status response also exposes the full project snapshot for programmatic inspection. (7 October 2026)

- A historical Create folder can differ from the V2 canonical folder `pages/ZenRayAssets/<id>`. Do not pass the old folder into the V2 project: normalizeWorkspaceProject refuses it. Preserve the old catalogue entry and its bytes, link its ID through `legacyProjectIds`, and let V2 generate its new source-scoped destination. The existing workspace view merges legacy metadata using these aliases; this does not move or prove historical files. (7 October 2026)
